# supergit workspace state — normally lives in the workspace dir
# (~/supergit/workspaces/<name>/), NEVER in this (public) repo. This is a
# defensive guard against an accidental commit if the daemon is ever pointed
# at a workspace inside the repo tree (e.g. SUPERGIT_WORKSPACE=./scratch).
# These files can contain private project paths and prompts. Force-add with
# `git add -f` if you ever genuinely need a file by one of these names.
tasks.json
repos.json
prefs.json
events.jsonl
session-titles.json
remote-daemons.json
*.json.tmp
